-- title:
--   Level-q automorphisms fix every prime below a supersingular point
-- statement:
--   **Arithmetic data.** Let $q$ and $\ell$ be primes, let $M'$ be a non-zero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and assume $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero, $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity, and assume (`hι`) that there is a ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\zeta) = e^{2\pi i/q}$. Let $H_1 \le (\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ be the subgroup [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22) $\cap$ $\ker\big((\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^\times\big)$, where `levelH q M'` is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$; thus $H_1$ consists of the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$ and modulo $\ell$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}(L)$, equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') H₁)`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), that is, the field generated over $L$ by the image under the coefficient embedding [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ over $\mathbb{Q}$.
--
--   Let $A$ be a henselian discrete valuation ring which is an $L$-subalgebra-base in the sense that $L$ is its fraction field, with algebraically closed residue field, with $q \in \mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hAq`) and with $\zeta$ in the image of $A$ (`hζA`); $K$ is an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. Let $j \in K$ be non-zero with Laurent expansion [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81), i.e. the $q$-expansion of the modular $j$-function. Let $\varpi$ generate $\mathfrak{m}_A$, and let $\varpi_t \in A$ satisfy $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q u$ for some unit $u$ (`hϖt`).
--
--   Write $C :=$ `chartAlgFin A ↥K j` for the integral closure of $A[j]$ in $K$ (the elements of $K$ integral over `Algebra.adjoin A {j}`), `jChartFin A ↥K j` for $j$ viewed in $C$, `XFin A ↥K j` $= \operatorname{Spec} C$, and [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A ↥K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) for the pushout of $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the two chart inclusions (the $j$-finite and the $j^{-1}$-finite chart), with `toBase` its structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ and `ιFin` the canonical morphism from `XFin` into the model. Let $y \subset C$ be a maximal ideal containing $\varpi$ (`hy`, `hϖy`) which is supersingular in the sense (`hss`) that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : C \to \Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of those $j_0 \in \Omega$ such that every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $j_0$ has no non-zero $q$-torsion point.
--
--   Throughout, for $\gamma \in \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ the phrase "$\tau$ is a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$" abbreviates [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L q ζ q (q ^ 2 * M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29) for $\tau \in \mathrm{Aut}_L(K)$: for every weight $k$, every pair of modular forms $f,g$ for $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ viewed in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$, with integral $q$-expansions $p_f, p_g$ and with the Laurent series of $p_g$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ non-zero, every $x \in K$ whose Laurent expansion is the image under `coeffEmb L` of that quotient of series, and every $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\zeta) = e^{2\pi i / q}$, one has $\iota_*\big((\tau x)\big) \cdot (g \mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\, q\, \gamma^{-1})^{\wedge} = (f \mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\, q\, \gamma^{-1})^{\wedge}$ as series, where ${}^{\wedge}$ denotes the $q$-expansion and $\mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\delta$ is the matrix with rows $(\delta_{00},\ \delta_{01}/q)$ and $(q\delta_{10},\ \delta_{11})$.
--
--   **The Drinfeld chart hypothesis `hArig`.** For every point $z$ of the two-chart model, every stalk element $\varpi_z$ equal to the germ at $z$ of the global section coming from $\varpi$ along `toBase`, lying in the maximal ideal of the stalk, every point $y'$ of `XFin` with `ιFin` image $z$ and satisfying the supersingularity condition of `hss` for $y'$, there exist a complete discrete valuation ring, a ring homomorphism $\sigma$ from $A$ to it carrying $\varpi$ to a generator of its maximal ideal, power series $f,u,v$ in two variables over it with $u,v$ units and $f \equiv X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$ (the Drinfeld form [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18)), and an isomorphism $e$ from the adic completion of the stalk at $z$ onto $S := W[[X_0,X_1]]/\big(C(\sigma(\varpi_t^{q+1}))\,v - f u\big)$, such that, writing $\mathrm{toC}$ for the map from the stalk to its completion, $\mathrm{mkS}$ for the quotient map onto $S$ and $\mathrm{germY}$ for the composite $C \to$ stalk at $z$ through the $\operatorname{Spec}$–$\Gamma$ adjunction and the germ on the open image of `ιFin`, the following seven clauses hold: (i) $e$ carries the germ of each $a \in A$ to the class of the constant $C(\sigma a)$; (ii) every level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ maps $C$ into $C$; (iii) if moreover $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod \ell$, then the induced endomorphism of $C$ is the identity modulo $y'$; (iv) for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, a level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $C$ and acting trivially modulo $y'$, there are a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an element $c$ and a $2 \times 2$ matrix $M$ over the coefficient ring such that $\theta$ transports the completed germ map along $\tau$, $\theta$ fixes all constants, $\theta(X_{j}) \equiv \sum_i M_{ij}X_i$ modulo the square of the ideal generated by the classes of $X_0, X_1$, $c^{q+1} \equiv 1$, $M_{ij} \equiv c\,\gamma_{ij}$ for all $i,j$, and $c \equiv 1$ whenever $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod \ell$, while $c \not\equiv 1$ whenever $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity (all congruences modulo the maximal ideal of the coefficient ring); (v) for integers $a_1,b_1,a_2,b_2$ and primes $P_1, P_2$ of $S$, each containing the class of $C(\sigma\varpi)$, each omitting the class of $X_0$ or of $X_1$, and each containing an element $a_iX_0 + b_iX_1 + h$ with $h \in (X_0,X_1)^2$, if $q \nmid a_1b_2 - a_2b_1$ then $P_1$ and $P_2$ have distinct pullbacks along $e \circ \mathrm{toC}$; (vi) for a prime $P$ of $S$ omitting the class of $X_0$ or of $X_1$, containing the class of $C(\sigma\varpi)$ and containing some $X_0 + h$ with $h \in (X_0,X_1)^2$, an element $a \in C$ has $\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}(a))$ in the pullback of $P$ along $e$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in the image of $\mathfrak{m}_A$ in $L$; (vii) the element [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) — the image of the $j$-series under the exponent-scaling `qExpand L q` — lies in $K$ and in $C$, and there are $a_0 \in A$ with $\mathrm{jqNModC} - a_0 \in y'$, an integer $e_0 \ge 1$ and $h \in (X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ whose degree-$e_0$ form is non-degenerate in the sense that $\sum_{i=0}^{e_0} (\text{coefficient of } X_0^iX_1^{e_0-i} \text{ in } h)\,a^i b^{e_0-i}$ is a unit for all $a,b$ with $a$ or $b$ a unit and $a^qb - ab^q$ in the maximal ideal, and such that $e(\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}(\mathrm{jqNModC} - a_0))) = \mathrm{mkS}(h)$.
--
--   **The chosen point and its explicit chart.** Let $z$, $\varpi_z$, $y'$ be as in the hypotheses of `hArig` (germ condition `hϖz`, maximality `hz`, `hy' : ιFin y' = z`, supersingularity `hss'`), with $y'$ cutting out exactly $y$ (`hy'y`). Let $W_1$ be a complete discrete valuation domain, $\sigma_1 : A \to W_1$ with $\mathfrak{m}_{W_1} = (\sigma_1\varpi)$, let $f_1, u_1, v_1$ be two-variable power series over $W_1$ with $u_1, v_1$ units and $f_1$ congruent to the Drinfeld form modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and let $e_1$ be an isomorphism from the adic completion of the stalk at $z$ onto $S := W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/\big(C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{q+1}))v_1 - f_1u_1\big)$. The hypothesis `hW₁` asserts for these data exactly the seven clauses (i)–(vii) listed above.
--
--   **The blown-up algebra and the valuation ring.** Let $J \subseteq C$ be the infimum (`hJ`) of the family of ideals obtained as follows: for $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $C$, take the pullback along the induced endomorphism of $C$ of the pullback along $e_1 \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germY}$ of the ideal of $S$ generated by the classes of $C(\sigma_1\varpi_t)$, $X_0$ and $X_1$. Let $B$ be the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ obtained (`hB`) by adjoining to $C$ all $x \in K$ with $x\varpi_t \in J$. Let $W$ be a valuation subring of $K$ containing $B$ (`hBW`).
--
--   The hypothesis `hR1` states that $C \subseteq B$ and that every element of $K$ is a quotient of two elements of $B$ with non-zero denominator. The hypothesis `hR2` states that $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A$ and that $B/\varpi B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$. The hypothesis `hR3` (five clauses) states that an element of $L$ lies in $W$ exactly when it comes from $A$; that $\mathfrak{m}_W$ is generated by $\varpi$; that $W$ is a discrete valuation ring; that an element of $C$ lies in $y$ exactly when it lies in $\mathfrak{m}_W$; and that $f \in K$ lies in $W$ exactly when $f = g/h$ with $g,h \in B$ and $h \notin \mathfrak{m}_W$.
--
--   The hypothesis `hEQ` (five clauses) states: for every $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$-algebra structure on the residue field $k$ of $A$ there is a surjective ring homomorphism $\rho : B \to$ [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q k`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) $= k[X_0,X_1]/(\mathrm{drinfeldPoly} - 1)$ whose kernel is exactly $B \cap \mathfrak{m}_W$, which is compatible with $A \to k$, and which is equivariant in the following sense: for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and a level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\tau(W) = W$ there exist $c \in \mathbb{F}_{q^2}^\times$ with $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, c)$ in [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) — the kernel of $(g,c) \mapsto \det(g)c^{q+1}$ — such that $\rho \circ \tau = \mathrm{hAction}(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,c) \circ \rho$ on $B$, and $c \ne 1$ whenever $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \ne \mathrm{id}$; secondly, every level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ preserves $B$; thirdly, for every prime $Q$ of $B$ containing $\varpi$ there are $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and a level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ carrying $B \cap \mathfrak{m}_W$ into $Q$; fourthly, if $b \in B$ is such that $\tau(b) \in \mathfrak{m}_W$ for all $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and all level automorphisms $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$, then $\varpi \mid b$ in $B$; fifthly, for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and a level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$, if $\tau$ preserves $y$ (on elements of $C$ whose $\tau$-image lies in $C$) then $\tau$ preserves $W$.
--
--   **The chosen automorphism and the conclusion.** Let $\gamma_0 \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and let $\tau_0$ be a level automorphism at $\gamma_0^{-1}$ with $f \in W \iff \tau_0 f \in W$ for all $f \in K$ (`hτ₀W`).
--
--   Then for every ideal $\mathfrak{p}$ of $C$ which is prime, contains $\varpi$, and satisfies $\mathfrak{p} \subseteq y$ and $\mathfrak{p} \ne y$, and for every $c \in C$ with $\tau_0(c) \in C$, one has $c \in \mathfrak{p}$ if and only if $\tau_0(c) \in \mathfrak{p}$. In other words, $\tau_0$ stabilises every prime of the $j$-finite chart algebra lying over $\varpi$ and strictly below the supersingular maximal ideal $y$.
--
--   This is the step asserting that the level-$q$ automorphisms act trivially on the set of branches (Igusa components) of the reduction of the modular curve $X_{H_1}(q^2M')$ through a supersingular point: each prime of the $j$-finite chart algebra over $\varpi$ strictly contained in the supersingular maximal ideal is preserved. It is the $\Gamma_1(\ell)$-diamond variant of the same statement, valid for all primes $q$, and it feeds the analysis of the blown-up chart in [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.exists_finset_ends_iff_isLocalization_blowupChart_card_eq_of_eq_adjoin_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.exists_finset_ends_iff_isLocalization_blowupChart_card_eq_of_eq_adjoin_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked_of_dvd); it is proved from the Igusa-valuation criterion [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.forall_mem_iff_map_mem_igusaValuation_of_isLevelAutAt_gamma_of_drinfeldChartWitness_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.forall_mem_iff_map_mem_igusaValuation_of_isLevelAutAt_gamma_of_drinfeldChartWitness_of_dvd).
